WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.601
-Kenan, I wanted
to ask you about this.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.567
This is very, very cool.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.667
Demi, I don't know
if you saw this.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.133
-I did see that.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.767
-Kenan got a star on
the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.267
-Oh!

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.200
Yeah. That was awesome.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.167
-I couldn't be happier
for you, bud.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.534
What was --
-Peep the bowtie.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.133
-Yeah, looking --
You're looking sharp.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.000
But, I mean, that's
an amazing accomplishment.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.267
-It looks like I left there
and started selling bean pies.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.501
-Yeah, no, no.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.000
Did -- Did you --
What was it like?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.267
What's the vibe there, though?

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.200
-You know, it was --
it was amazing.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.067
It was very surreal.
My whole family was there.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.033
You know, generations of family
and stuff like that.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.934
So it was just very touching.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:38.567
It was hot.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.501
-You could -- You could see it
on my little one's face.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:41.567
Like, she was not having it.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.767
-She was like,
"This is just too hot.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.133
Hurry -- Hurry this up."
-She was over it.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.234
Yeah, she wanted
chicken fingers.

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.934
So...
-Yeah, yeah. She did.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.701
You sent me a picture,
which I am glad.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.200
Because you're on
the carpet here.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.767
Look. Isn't this nice?
You're wearing the bowtie.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.934
You got the thing and the star
and the red carpet.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.501
-The red carpet out there.
That's nice.

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.667
-Yeah, and then, under the red
carpet, you see this poking out.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.968
-Yeah, on the side.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.701
-That's Lorne Michaels.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.167
-Yes.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.234
-How disrespectful.
How disrespectful...

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.734
-Yeah, it seemed real dis--
Just half-covered.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.067
-...to the great Lorne Michaels.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.801
-Yeah, that's just --
That's cold, Lorne Michaels.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.634
-He got Phantom of the Opera'd.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.067
-He got Phantom'd.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:15.601
-Cover the whole thing up.
You know?

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.801
-Yeah, don't even let you know
that you're over Lorne's star.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.467
-Peeking at me. It's weird.
He's always watching.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:21.267
-But you're next to --
You're next to Lorne's star.

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:22.734
-Yeah, it's crazy.
-That's kind of cool.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:23.901
-It's unbelievable, man.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.267
Like, I mean,
when are you getting yours?

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:27.601
You're getting yours...?

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:28.868
[ Audience oohs ]
...soon?

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.801
I'm genuinely --
I'm genuinely asking.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.801
-Yeah, they told me
that they were full.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:33.968
-They're full up?

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.501
-They told me that
the sidewalk was full.

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:36.667
-I saw a couple of spaces.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.334
-They said,
"We have enough stars, yeah."

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.767
-I'm gonna go ahead and advocate
for Jimmy to get his star ASAP.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.334
Am I right?

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I mean, yeah.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.567
-You've put in more work
than I have.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:45.767
-I put some work in, right?
-I'm here for it.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.267
-But I didn't --
I'll tell you what I didn't do.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.801
-What?
-"Good Burger."

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:52.734
-Oh, look at the "Good Burger"
little kiddy faces.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.434
Look at those little babies.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:57.067
-I have to say, I had this
on an orange VHS tape.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.968
-You had the orange tape?
-Yes, I had the orange tape.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.534
-Oh, amazing.
-That's legit. That's real.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:01.534
-Yes. Yes.
-Nickelodeon.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.367
-VHS tapes were a way for...

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.701
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. They understand.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.767
-...people to watch movies
in the '90s, yeah.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.734
-And this is 25 years ago.
-Yeah, that's crazy.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:12.000
Anybody feeling old yet?
-No.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.367
-When you first met
Kel Mitchell,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.901
when you got together,
did you go,

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.367
"Oh, we got a little chemistry"?

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.567
Did you feel like, "Oh,
we're gonna be funny together"?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.901
-When we started
working together, because, like,

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:24.367
we were kids, so we had school
at first, and I was a nerd.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.767
So, like, all the other kids
had met each other.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.834
They had, like, a pizza party,
and I was hired kind of last,

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.567
so I missed all the, like,
introduction night or whatever.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.200
-Oh, no!

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.033
-So, my first --
my first day was that morning.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.801
And, you know, everybody was
just doing their school work,

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.267
and I was super quiet, so
everybody was looking at me

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.234
like I was standoffish
or -- or whatever.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.400
And then we started rehearsing.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.434
And we did these characters
called Mavis and Clavis,

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.367
which were these two
kind of, like,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.868
old Black guys in a balcony,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.200
like, heckling people
or whatever.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.834
-Mavis and Clavis.
-Mavis and Clavis.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.701
And, yeah, we've been --
-Two friends.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.167
Their names happen
to rhyme with each other.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Never met each other.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.868
They just came together. 'Cause
it's -- it's sketch comedy.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.734
-"Yeah, that's interesting.
Your name rhymes with mine."

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.067
-Yeah, and I just
immediately recognized

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.434
that he was brilliant, you know?

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:05.801
And we were very similar,

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.400
so then we just hit it off
from that point.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.634
So it was very much
a day-one kind of thing.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:14.300
-Yeah. I know this is
a little cryptic here, but...

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.400
At the bottom, it says,
"What's up with that part two?"

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.934
-Yeah, what's up
with that part two?

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.767
You know what I'm saying? What's
up with that sequel there?

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.501
You know what I mean?
-Wait. So what are you saying?

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.000
-Yes!
-Are you saying --

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.934
Are you saying that
"Good Burger 2" is happening?

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.734
-I would like it to.

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.133
-Okay.
[ Drum roll stops abruptly ]

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.534
That's very anticlimactic.
-Very anti--

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.067
"I would love to annou--"

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.934
No, we are, you know, working
harder on it than -- than ever.

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.534
So it's about, you know,
meeting the numbers,

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.501
letting the numbers match up,
'cause I need them numbers.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.834
You know what I'm talking about.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:49.467
-Oh, stop it. You're not
even looking at anyone.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.200
You weren't even looking at --

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.534
-You guys --
You guys feel me, right?

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.234
-There's no one there.
Do you have an idea for it?

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.968
-You know the numbers
I need, man.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.767
-Do you have any idea
of what it would be about?

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:01.200
-Uh --
-No.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.767
-I feel like Kel should have,
like, a million kids.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.267
Like, Ed's character should
have, like, a million kids.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.100
And then, like, I'm coming out
of jail for something

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.567
that he put me in jail for.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:09.901
-That he did and you -- yeah.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.968
And he had a great life.
You went to prison. Yeah, yeah.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.067
Can you believe that you're
going into the 20th season

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.267
of "Saturday Night Live"?

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.234
Two-zero.
-Yeah. Two-zero. It's crazy.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.901
20 years.
-This is legendary status.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:22.934
Legendary status.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:25.701
-I mean, I agree with you, sir.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.300
It is legendary status.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.834
I don't know how to, like,
process that, man.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.634
You know what I'm saying?
It's still all about, like --

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.000
-I mean, we were there --
How do you --

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.367
Do you remember the years
we were together?

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:35.834
-It was only one year.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.267
Like, I remember you being

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.868
the biggest damn near rock star
on the show.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:42.400
You know what I'm saying? Like,
you didn't really do much work.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.834
Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:47.234
-That's why I want my star
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:49.267
-Only because
you were so seasoned at --

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:51.400
You could just come, float in,
do whatever you wanted,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.734
and, like, that was cool.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.467
Like, you didn't even feel
the pressures of anything.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:56.434
Like, you did --
We did a "Grease" sketch

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:57.801
where you had to sing, like,

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.267
that super high-pitched
John Travolta.

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.734
And you -- you crushed that.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.434
Like, not a lot of people
can squeak up that "high."

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.968
♪ High ♪
You know what I'm talking about?

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-And it was you and Tina.

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:10.434
And y'all just seemed like y'all
were married, and that was cool

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.968
and just, like, best friends.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:15.100
-And it was --
it was an interesting,

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.868
like, brotherhood to join.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.434
Brotherhood/sisterhood.
-Yeah.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:19.934
-And I was so happy
that y'all were like

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:21.534
my -- my older siblings.
You know, I have such --

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:22.701
-And then I left you
in the dust.

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.234
-In the dust. Completely.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.834
And went to do, like,
mad movies.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:28.234
-Yeah, I said,
"Son, take care of this place."

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:29.968
-Yeah, and then you came --
you came back home.

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.767
-I came back home.
-Right to the sixth floor.

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.534
-I did.
-We're -- We're right upstairs.

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:36.067
-I see you all the time. I'm
always rooting for you, buddy.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:38.934
-Nice having you back home, Dad.
Thanks.

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.200
It's good. Good times.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.434
-I promised I wouldn't cry.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.868
-I promised everyone
I wouldn't cry.

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:48.367
Can we talk about the Emmys?
-Let's talk about the Emmys.

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:49.868
I'm hosting it.
-You're hosting the Emmys.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.601
-Bing, bong, bang! Yeah.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:56.167
-You've won on Emmy.
You've been nominated for Emmys.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.501
Do you remember
first going to the Emmys?

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.434
-Yeah, my first time
actually going, I had to open

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:04.100
the show with Kate doing
this, like, song and dance.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.267
And we --
-Oh, yeah. I remember that.

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:07.834
-Yeah, with, like,
all the other, like, I think --

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.868
I want to say
NBC kind of talent.

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:12.868
And it was, like,
a full-on week of rehearsal.

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:14.801
And we had just won
the previous week.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:16.200
-That's your first time
at the Emmys.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.400
-My first time.
-You opened it.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.801
-So it was like
a two-week experience.

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:20.234
We won at the Creative Emmys

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.133
the week before
for "Come Back, Barack."

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.701
And then, yeah, we --

00:06:23.701 --> 00:06:25.567
My first time going,
I had to open the show.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.734
Big, big-ass stage. Crazy.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:29.167
-What do you think
are the ingredients

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:31.033
for a good awards show?

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:33.767
-Not to bore everybody like
I hope I'm not doing right now.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.267
-No.
-No.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:37.567
-Yeah, 'cause it gets
kind of redundant, I guess.

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.734
You know there's gonna be, like,
20, 30 awards or something.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:41.834
So you don't want people to,
like, you know, get up there

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.901
like the NBA draft
and they're like,

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:46.234
"I want to thank God,
my family, and, you know.

00:06:46.234 --> 00:06:47.767
I want to try hard."

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:49.534
You know,
like that Bill Burr joke.

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:52.734
But it's my job to, like,
keep everything fresh and hype

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:56.367
and, you know, celebrating,
you know, artistic creativity.

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:58.801
-I don't think they could have
picked a better human

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:00.234
to host this.
-Oh, man. Thank you, man.

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:01.601
-Kenan Thompson.
Congratulations.

00:07:01.601 --> 00:07:03.367
-Thank you very much.
Thank you very much.

00:07:03.367 --> 00:07:04.834
-Kenan Thompson, everybody.

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:07.734
Hosting the Emmys, live,
September 12th on NBC.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.434
They're also streaming
on Peacock.

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:11.367
-Right.
-Jeremy Allen White

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:13.133
joins us after the break.
Stick around, everybody.

